    "result_text": "The screen now has a header with the counters, and all 4 acceptance tests pass in `bin/e2e`.\n\n**What it shows:**\n- The number of people on the sheet, including retired people.\n- How many claims are in each status: DRAFT, OPEN, PENDING, SETTLED and VOID.\n- The sheet's due-total and overdue-total.\n\n**How it stays equal to the figures it repeats:** the header doesn't compute anything itself. It takes the same values that already feed the summary's status counts and the sheet's due and overdue totals. The \"Show retired\" toggle has no effect on it.\n\n**Where it lives:** the header is a new component in `src/main/frontend/src/app/features/summary/sheet-header.ts`, placed at the top of the people screen in `features/people/people.ts`. I didn't change the server or the stored data, because everything the header needs was already loaded on the front end.\n\n**One limit to \"shown at all times\":** the header appears whenever a sheet is loaded, but not on the empty \"Nothing here yet\" screen before one is. Counters wouldn't mean anything there, and the tests always load a sheet first. If you want it visible on that screen too, showing zeros, it's a small change.",
